# @summary pkg's FETCH_TIMEOUT in seconds for the packages of a bake (image pkg install). pkg 2.9 (libfetch) uses it as the connect timeout and as the stall watch: a fetch that stays under 2 KB/s for this long is abandoned (fetch_libfetch.c, fetchSpeedLimit/fetchSpeedTime), the size of the file plays no part. pkg's default of 30 ended a 2.8 GB texlive-docs after 600 MB on a slow uplink on 13.11.2026; five minutes rides out a short stall, and a connection that is dead costs five minutes, not an hour, before the next try of VM_BAKE_PKG_INSTALL_TRIES takes over from the cache.
